[phases] order lists a slug that is not a phase. A phase file that does not
parse still counts as a phase.

-- ajiya.toml --
[project]
name = "Fixture"
prefix = "FX"

[phases]
order = ["core", "gone", "broken"]
-- ajiya/core.md --
<!-- Written by ajiya. Do not edit by hand: use ajiya commands. -->
# Core

Goal: g

| ID | App | Ticket | Done when | Depends | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| FX-0001 | infra | Schema | a | - | 🟥 Pending |
-- ajiya/broken.md --
not a phase file
-- want --
E013 ajiya.toml: [phases] order lists "gone", which is not a phase. Fix: remove "gone" from [phases] order in ajiya.toml, or add it with 'ajiya phase add gone "<goal>"'
E001 ajiya/broken.md:1: expected the phase title as "# <title>". Fix: restore it with 'git checkout -- ajiya/broken.md' and make the change with ajiya commands
